        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: il carabiniere",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "il carabiniere — \"the carabiniere, the military police officer\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ho chiesto aiuto a un carabiniere. I asked a carabiniere for help."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One of the two main police forces; the other is la polizia."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "carabiniere is usually traced to French carabinier, a soldier armed with a carabine, a short gun. EtymDB derives carabine from carabin \"a dragoon\", whose own origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
